{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>For YHWH your Elohim has blessed you</b> — therefore do not deny His goodness so as to appear as though you are poor, but rather show yourselves to be rich. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Deuteronomy 2:7). But I do not understand what <b>in all the work of your hands</b> means, for the blessings with which they were blessed were blessings of heaven, and they would not make anything with their hands that could be blessed. Perhaps <b>the work of your hands</b> alludes to the fact that the flocks and cattle they brought out of Egypt were blessed along with them, and they possess wealth and cattle and property from the spoil of Egypt and from the spoil of Amalek, and everything was blessed in their hand — as in the verse, <i>the work of Your hands You have blessed, and his livestock has increased in the land</i> (Job 1:10). Furthermore, <b>YHWH has known your walking through this great wilderness</b>, and He supplied there all your needs with the manna and the quail and the waters of the well, so that you lacked nothing of what is necessary for those who travel the roads. And indeed it was so, for they purchased food and provisions from the children of Esau, as it says (below, verses 28–29), <i>Food for money you shall sell me and I will eat, and water for money you shall give me and I will drink</i>, and so on — <i>as the children of Esau did for me</i>, and so on."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:44:23.258653713Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}